{{also|implaçable}}
==English==
{{was wotd|2019|April|17}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|implācāble||immitigable, unappeasable}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=implācāble|part of speech=adj|id=MED22196|accessdate=4 December 2018}}</ref> or {{der|en|fro|implacable||harsh, unrelenting; implacable}} (modern {{cog|fr|implacable}}), both from {{der|en|la|implācābilis||unappeasable, implacable; irreconcilable}}, from {{m|la|im-}} (variant of {{m|la|in-||''prefix meaning ‘not’''}}) + {{m|la|plācābilis||placable; appeasing, moderating, pacifying, propitiating; acceptable}} (from {{m|la|plācō||to assuage, pacify, placate; to appease; to reconcile}} + {{m|la|-bilis||''suffix forming adjectives indicating a capacity or worth of being acted upon''}}).<ref>{{R:OED Online|part of speech=adj|id=92421|date=1899}}</ref>

